{"title":"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has parallel sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c337e833a82ec0650a1a82a4443a76307ebe7c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The other two sides are of lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are acute. What is the length of the shorter diagonal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0aed7d897ce38d40ac5bf7c7d26a214b63ba3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }10\\sqrt{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }25\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }8\\sqrt{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }18\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"471\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9ca0851053447734faf67e2fea554d233570a13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pair A,B,C,D,CC,DD; A = (-2,7); B = (14,7); C = (10,0); D = (0,0); CC = (10,7); DD = (0,7); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); //label(&quot;33&quot;,(A+B)/2,N); label(&quot;21&quot;,(C+D)/2,S); label(&quot;10&quot;,(A+D)/2,W); label(&quot;14&quot;,(B+C)/2,E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,DD,N); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,CC,N); draw(C--CC); draw(D--DD); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"172\" />\n</p><p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/82304399561c9bbbd28355f0001538d85e5fcdd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE} \\perp \\overline{AB}, \\overline{FC} \\perp \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />. \nDenote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edd8e7c503014899bfa7079243ea69ab00a33998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE} = x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb0ff07868f6a99309fa2a1aee14913ad6f9da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE} = h$\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />. In right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we have from the Pythagorean theorem: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbe5bda57187178092f83408440794bfcb46f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+h^2=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e66384f6436471e6db2fc5b83b070d37139f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = DC$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e4bed409872576b489f0989ba3125adb639214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = 33-DC-x = 12-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"230\" height=\"13\" />. Using the Pythagorean theorem in right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efdd26b7cbfad505c1adbdfccc28d3ab1eb91872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2cc51f6f2244f6fdd290377e06e3d357edc6de0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12-x)^2 + h^2 = 196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nWe isolate the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319c4d6557b81962a2076f2017878709cf698551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> term in both equations, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a1065d321fa2989d3caf0d15c0c9574087c56df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2= 100-x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff1ddacef6d6a27413c8ba66dc48283e9bc9028a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 = 196-(12-x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Setting these equal, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942906c980a60bf45f3ee51ec5db24fc5ef996f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100-x^2 = 196 - 144 + 24x -x^2 \\implies 24x = 48 \\implies x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"472\" height=\"16\" />. Now, we can determine that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/8696119ba2d8f3c2e29747818af22f124d45d0db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 = 100-4 \\implies h = 4\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e6521da560e1ec7a858424e7feccb41d363af4d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pair A,B,C,D,CC,DD; A = (-2,7); B = (14,7); C = (10,0); D = (0,0); CC = (10,7); DD = (0,7); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); //label(&quot;33&quot;,(A+B)/2,N); label(&quot;21&quot;,(C+D)/2,S); label(&quot;10&quot;,(A+D)/2,W); label(&quot;14&quot;,(B+C)/2,E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,DD,SE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,CC,SW); draw(C--CC); draw(D--DD); label(&quot;21&quot;,(CC+DD)/2,N); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(A+DD)/2,N); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(CC+B)/2,N); label(&quot;$4\\sqrt{6}$&quot;,(C+CC)/2,W); label(&quot;$4\\sqrt{6}$&quot;,(D+DD)/2,E); pair X = (-2,0); //draw(X--C--A--cycle,black+2bp); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>The two diagonals are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Using the Pythagorean theorem again on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf1a9b5d47656f521d715d9b85bd2c2d9490473.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup AFC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2da1bcd0c5138dfe5f66d1ebe0b46542ed6bbc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup BED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, we can find these lengths to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca34bc631b783aecc29ef49389a73f0977498c5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{96+529} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d1b476bae5560ab678ab869fae8ff794f94e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{96+961} = \\sqrt{1057}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc04297061c012b247afae1b71fd2b70971bdd21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{96+529}&lt;\\sqrt{96+961}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is the shorter length*, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3d885331dfd1c95d782aac3adccec7dd046fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Or, alternatively, one can notice that the two triangles have the same height but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf1a9b5d47656f521d715d9b85bd2c2d9490473.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup AFC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> has a shorter base than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2da1bcd0c5138dfe5f66d1ebe0b46542ed6bbc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup BED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba9cc897cd3d3cc662ace19dc67b9f53085f698.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pair A,B,C,D,E; A = (-2,7); B = (14,7); C = (10,0); D = (0,0); E = (4,7); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(D--E); label(&quot;21&quot;,(C+D)/2,S); label(&quot;10&quot;,(A+D)/2,W); label(&quot;14&quot;,(12,1),E); label(&quot;14&quot;,(2,1),E); label(&quot;12&quot;,(A+E)/2,N); label(&quot;21&quot;,(E+B)/2,N); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,N); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"172\" />\n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64782f3ed925c790fed487d26744eb0ed100f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is by Heron's, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5ca8160d993e3ec4abc00255c9ebd54e4a9fb3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{9(4)(3)(2)}=24\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"172\" height=\"32\" />. This makes the length of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/2/772b05fb973d72e457456b2a4cf59dce04562003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. One may now proceed as in Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to obtain an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3d885331dfd1c95d782aac3adccec7dd046fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the same way as Solution 1, obtain that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3b417b8f8d9016f5f0624e1617eca7f3caf1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and drop a perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Call this point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027e0ea8628cdffffa62af421dd7b03bc3f698ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GC=DC+AE=21+2=23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"251\" height=\"16\" />, and following the method from Solution 1, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4fbd8a97aa874b1589e8a54e1c0c8650c4d735d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG=4\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"21\" />. Thus the answer would be the \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b58694b7a205ceb3446a5b5c281aaa01d0d7f80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{23^2+(4\\sqrt{6})^2}=\\sqrt{529+96}=\\sqrt{625}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 25}\\]\" width=\"381\" height=\"34\" />\n-Reality Writes\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B\">2014 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2